{
  "id": "pim-eligible-access",
  "provider": "azure",
  "title": "PIM: eligible vs active access",
  "summary": "Eligible assignments (dashed) grant nothing until someone activates them for a limited time. They can target a role directly, or membership in a group that holds the role (PIM for Groups).",
  "notes": [
    "Direct path: the user is eligible for Contributor on the subscription. Activation can require MFA, a justification, and approval, and it expires (e.g. after 8h).",
    "Group path (PIM for Groups): the group holds a standing Owner assignment on one resource group, and the user is only an eligible member. This keeps role assignments stable while membership is just-in-time.",
    "Role assignments inherit down the scope tree: Contributor on the subscription also applies to every resource group under it."
  ],
  "docs": [
    {
      "title": "What is Privileged Identity Management?",
      "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/entra/id-governance/privileged-identity-management/pim-configure"
